      "hints": [
        "Take natural logarithms of both sides of $8^{3 - 6x} = 4 \\times 5^{-2x}$.",
        "Use logarithm laws $\\ln(AB) = \\ln A + \\ln B$ and $\\ln(A^B) = B\\ln A$ to form a linear equation in $x$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Take the natural logarithm of both sides of the equation:\n$$\\ln\\left(8^{3 - 6x}\\right) = \\ln\\left(4 \\times 5^{-2x}\\right)$$",
        "Apply the product law $\\ln(uv) = \\ln u + \\ln v$ and power law $\\ln(u^v) = v\\ln u$:\n$$(3 - 6x)\\ln 8 = \\ln 4 + \\ln\\left(5^{-2x}\\right)$$\n$$(3 - 6x)\\ln 8 = \\ln 4 - 2x\\ln 5$$",
        "Expand the left-hand side:\n$$3\\ln 8 - 6x\\ln 8 = \\ln 4 - 2x\\ln 5$$",
        "Collect all terms in $x$ on the left-hand side and constants on the right-hand side:\n$$2x\\ln 5 - 6x\\ln 8 = \\ln 4 - 3\\ln 8$$\n$$x(2\\ln 5 - 6\\ln 8) = \\ln 4 - 3\\ln 8$$\nMultiply both sides by $-1$:\n$$x(6\\ln 8 - 2\\ln 5) = 3\\ln 8 - \\ln 4$$",
        "Isolate $x$:\n$$x = \\dfrac{3\\ln 8 - \\ln 4}{6\\ln 8 - 2\\ln 5}$$\nUsing $8 = 2^3$ and $4 = 2^2$:\n$$\\text{Numerator} = 3(3\\ln 2) - 2\\ln 2 = 9\\ln 2 - 2\\ln 2 = 7\\ln 2$$\n$$\\text{Denominator} = 6(3\\ln 2) - 2\\ln 5 = 18\\ln 2 - 2\\ln 5$$\n$$x = \\dfrac{7\\ln 2}{18\\ln 2 - 2\\ln 5}$$",
        "Evaluate the numerical expressions step by step:\n$$\\ln 2 \\approx 0.69314718$$\n$$\\ln 5 \\approx 1.60943791$$\n$$\\text{Numerator} = 7(0.69314718) = 4.85203026$$\n$$\\text{Denominator} = 18(0.69314718) - 2(1.60943791) = 12.47664924 - 3.21887582 = 9.25777342$$\n$$x = \\dfrac{4.85203026}{9.25777342} \\approx 0.52410339 \\dots$$",
        "Round correct to 3 decimal places:\n$$x = 0.524$$"
      ],
